/// Top-level OTP supervision tree for the Exdura durable workflow engine.
///
/// Five components are supervised children in dependency order:
///   1. EventStore — durable event persistence
///   2. ActivityWorkerPool — supervised activity execution
///   3. WorkflowEngine — workflow orchestration (resolves deps by name)
///   4. TimerManager — durable timer scheduling (resolves deps by name)
///   5. ExduraHttpServer — optional HTTP client API (SPEC.md §7.2)
///
/// Uses rest_for_one: if EventStore crashes, everything after it restarts.
/// If WorkflowEngine crashes, TimerManager and ExduraHttpServer restart too.
/// `ExduraHttpServer` is always present (bound to nothing is the normal,
/// cheap default, same as every other still-childless-equivalent resting
/// state in this tree); `ExduraWorker start:` durably records the
/// port/workflowClasses config on `EventStore` (`setHttpConfig:`) and
/// triggers `refreshFromDurableConfig` when `#http` config is given. Because that
/// config is durable rather than held in a process that a `rest_for_one`
/// cascade can wipe, ANY restart — cascade or a direct crash of
/// `ExduraHttpServer` itself — re-reads it and re-binds automatically; see
/// `ExduraHttpServer>>startListening` for the full mechanism. (An earlier
/// design routed this through a nested `DynamicSupervisor`
/// (`ExduraHttpServerSupervisor`) with args passed only once via
/// `startChild:` — a `rest_for_one` cascade tore down that dynamically-added
/// child with nothing to re-add it. Replaced once `ExduraHttpServer` could
/// resolve its own config durably, the same way the other four resolve
/// their collaborators by name below, instead of needing a second
/// supervisor layer to route runtime args around `class children`'s own
/// parameterless, once-evaluated signature.)
///
/// All five components are registered under fixed names (ADR 0079) and
/// resolve each other by name at use-time rather than caching pids — see
/// `WorkflowEngine>>eventStore`/`activityPool`,
/// `TimerManager>>engine`/`eventStore`, and `ExduraHttpServer>>initialize`.
/// This is deliberate: an earlier version wired dependencies once via a
/// `class initialize: sup` hook, documented as "re-runs on restart
/// (rest_for_one)" — that claim was wrong. `initialize:` fires exactly
/// once, at the initial `supervise` call; OTP-driven restarts start each
/// child directly and never call it again. A restarted `WorkflowEngine`
/// came back with a nil `eventStore` and crashed on the next workflow
/// call. Named lookup sidesteps the problem entirely — nothing needs to
/// notice a restart happened.
///
///   beamtalk run                          // starts via beamtalk.toml
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// sup := ExduraSupervisor supervise     // or start manually
/// ```
typed Supervisor subclass: ExduraSupervisor

  /// rest_for_one: if a child crashes, all children after it restart.
  class strategy -> Symbol => #restForOne

  /// Child specs in dependency order.
  ///
  /// All five register under fixed names (ADR 0079) so siblings — and
  /// external consumers like `ExduraClient` — can resolve them fresh after
  /// a restart instead of holding a pid captured at construction.
  /// `WorkflowEngine` additionally gets `#supervised => true` in its args:
  /// unlike EventStore, a nil `activityPool` field is also a legitimate
  /// standalone state (Phase 0, no-pool mode via `WorkflowEngine
  /// withStore:`), so it needs an explicit signal to know "nil means look
  /// it up by name" applies here. `ExduraHttpServer` needs no such args at
  /// all — a nil `engine`/`store`/`port`/`workflowClasses` always means
  /// "resolve me" for it (see its own `initialize`/`startListening`), no
  /// disambiguating flag required.
  ///
  /// Only one `ExduraSupervisor` may be alive at a time per node as a
  /// result of the fixed names; tests that spawn one must run serially
  /// (`class serial -> Boolean => true`).
  class children -> List =>
    storeSpec := EventStore supervisionSpec withName: #eventStore withRestart: #permanent
    poolSpec := ActivityWorkerPool supervisionSpec withName: #activityWorkerPool withRestart: #permanent
    engineSpec := (WorkflowEngine supervisionSpec)
      withName: #workflowEngine
      withRestart: #permanent
      withArgs: #{#supervised => true}
    timerSpec := TimerManager supervisionSpec withName: #timerManager withRestart: #permanent
    httpSpec := ExduraHttpServer supervisionSpec withName: #exduraHttpServer withRestart: #permanent

    #(storeSpec, poolSpec, engineSpec, timerSpec, httpSpec)
